{"availability":"available","full":"screentinker/screentinker","name":"screentinker","description":"Open-source digital signage management software. Control content on TVs, displays, and kiosks from anywhere.","category":"Other","language":"JavaScript","stars":178,"forks":48,"created":"2026-04-08T17:16:53Z","updated":"2026-10-09T20:23:32Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://screentinker.com","topics":["android-tv","cms","digital-signage","fire-tv","kiosk","nodejs","open-source","raspberry-pi","self-hosted","signage","sqlite"],"demo":"https://screentinker.com/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:58.310Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:58.310Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T23:11:58.310Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T23:11:58.310Z","stars":178,"forks":48}],"technologies":["Node.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Live demo · API reference · Self-hosting guide · Discord · What's new in 2.1 (video)","ScreenTinker is a free, open-source digital signage CMS you can self-host on your own server — or run in our managed cloud. Manage TVs, video walls, and kiosks across multiple locations from one dashboard, with remote control, scheduling, playlists, and analytics. Built for retail, QSR menu boards, offices, lobbies, education, and any environment where you need centralized control over remote screens. Multi-tenant, MIT-licensed, single-developer maintained with direct contact access.","Runs on any screen — Android TV, Fire TV, Samsung Tizen, LG webOS, Amazon Vega OS, Raspberry Pi, Windows, ChromeOS, or any web browser. No per-device player licence, no hardware lock-in."],"features":["Playlists — first-class playlist objects: create, reorder, set per-item duration, share one playlist across multiple displays; draft/publish workflow with revert-to-published","Slides — a built-in slide editor: build decks of slides with templates, fields, and per-element entrance animations, an optional voiceover per 